--TEST--
A `[limits]` value above the `[limits.hard]` ceiling written beside it stops the boot with E0601 — `rule:config/ceilings-are-their-own-directives`
--FILE nvs.toml--
[limits]
memory = "1G"

[limits.hard]
memory = "512M"
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A request may start with at most its ceiling, so the configuration is refused.
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0601]: `[limits] memory` is `1G`, which is above its ceiling of `512M`
%A
